# The measure

## What is re-derived here, and how

The counts that motivate the fix are issue #1082's own: 2 523 turns over the 8 newest items at a 15 649 tok/turn
baseline, ~11.6 k of it the composed prompt, ~29 Mtok of a 90.6 Mtok night. This change re-derives none of them. What
it does re-derive is the **size the fix moves**, three ways, so that a reader can put the before and the after side by
side:

1. the two skeletons, by `wc -c`;
2. the **composed** prompt, rendered the way `run.sh` renders it, over one value set — item #1030's own, taken from
   the prompt that item's run left behind — before and after the move;
3. the prompt the **case's own throwaway project** renders, read out of the case's failure text when a bound is set
   under it (the case only prints the size when it is over one).

The renderer is `loop_render` (`tools/loop/lib.sh:1163`): one accumulated string, one `KEY=VALUE` pair at a time, with
`patsub_replacement` off so a `&` in a section's text is a `&`. The harness below is that substitution and nothing else,
and it is validated against the archived prompt: rendered from `adb79f6f^`'s template — the one item #1030's run was
started with — it reproduces `.pi/issue-loop/items/1030/worker-prompt.md` **byte for byte**, 32 580 B.

```
$ cat /tmp/render1082.sh
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# /tmp/render1082.sh <template> <gate-step file> <out>
set -u
shopt -u patsub_replacement 2>/dev/null || true
TPL="$1"; STEP="$2"; OUT="$3"
item=/home/tim/projects/NaviVeylin/.pi/issue-loop/items/1030
tpl=$(cat "$TPL")
tpl="${tpl//\{\{GATE_STEP\}\}/$(cat "$STEP")}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{ISSUE\}\}/1030}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{CHANGE_ROOT\}\}//home/tim/projects/NaviVeylin/.pi/worktrees/loop}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{WORK_PACKAGE\}\}/$item/work-package.md}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{EVIDENCE_DIR\}\}/$item}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{SCRATCH_DIR\}\}/$item/scratch}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{BASE\}\}/ae2373cb001116c38ed70d1fad25ef7a1b3c3cbf}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{GATE_CMD\}\}/.\/tools\/loop\/gate.sh}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{MEASURE_CMD\}\}/.\/tools\/loop\/measure.sh}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{WORKER_SKILLS\}\}/openspec-propose openspec-apply-change build-app run-tests revert-check}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{CLASS\}\}/bug}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{PROPOSE_CLASS\}\}/feature}"
tpl="${tpl//\{\{WORKER_REFERENCE\}\}/$item/worker-reference.md}"
printf '%s\n' "$tpl" > "$OUT"
```

