**32 674 B → 27 112 B, 5 562 B less per turn** on item #1030's own paths. The 94 B between 32 580 and 32 674 is the
sentence issue #1083 added to the shell-refusal block after item #1030 ran, so the archived prompt stands 5 468 B above
the fixed one and the tree this fix lands on stands 5 562 B above it. At ~2 500 turns an item that is ~13.9 MB of
re-sent prompt per item, ~1 980 tok a turn at the ~11.6 k-per-32 580 B the issue's baseline was taken at — ~13 % of a
15 649 tok/turn turn, which is the −10…−13 % the issue claims and not the −26 % halving the prompt would give.

## The prompt the case's own fixture renders

The case's throwaway project sits deeper than a run's item directory (a suite scratch root, a case directory, the
fixture repository), so it renders larger than the item figure above. The case prints its size only when the bound is
under it, so both readings come from a failure run:

- on the **base**, with `LOOP_WORKER_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES=29000` added to the base's `loop.conf`
  (`evidence/red-on-base.log`, second block):
  `the composed worker prompt is 33726 B, over the recorded bound of 29000 B (LOOP_WORKER_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES)`;
- on the **fixed** tree, with the key temporarily set to `20000` and put back to `29000` afterwards:
  `the composed worker prompt is 28389 B, over the recorded bound of 20000 B (LOOP_WORKER_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES)`.

**33 726 B → 28 389 B, 5 337 B less per turn**, against a bound of 29 000 B: **611 B of headroom** on the deepest render
this tree produces. That headroom is the number to read the bound with — a paragraph added to `worker.md` that costs
more than 611 B on the fixture's paths crosses it and the run says so.

## What the two figures in the fix's own text measure

The fix commit's message states 32 580 B → 27 073 B (−5 507 B), and the comment over `LOOP_WORKER_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES` in
`loop.conf` states "fell to 26 385 B" with "10 130 B it no longer carries". None of those four numbers re-renders from
this tree by either method above: the rendered pairs are 32 674 → 27 112 and 33 726 → 28 389, and the bytes the prompt
no longer carries are 5 727 B of template, 5 562 B of the item's composed prompt and 5 337 B of the fixture's. The
measured figures are the ones this archive's evidence holds; correcting the two sentences in the merged fix is a
change of its own, and the 611 B headroom is what that correction should be written against.

Read: the prompt a turn re-reads fell by ~5.4 kB on both renders, the reference that carries the rest is charged once
per item rather than once per turn, and the size that is still charged on every turn is a number a run records, prints
beside its other bounds and compares the rendered file against.
